15. Programming Round
Q: Count increasing digit substring from a large number. long n = 269253001778 → Ans: 5

#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    long n = 269253001778;
    int prev, curr, count = 0;

    prev = n % 10;
    n = n / 10;

    while (n > 0) {
        curr = n % 10;
        if (curr < prev)
            count++;
        prev = curr;
        n = n / 10;
    }

    printf("Count = %d", count);
    return 0;
}
This walks the digits from least-significant to most-significant and counts how many times a digit is smaller than the one before it in that direction — equivalent to counting "ascending steps" when the number is read left-to-right. For this input it evaluates to 5, matching the expected answer.

